    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Although debriefing has proved to be a highly effective learning strategy, it is currently widely adopted only in a small number of learning settings. Debriefly aims to change this by making debriefing more accessible and relevant for new contexts. As part of this project, a first version of Debriefly was developed around a specific learning goal: reparation for GRE math sections. Learners experienced a facilitated debriefing process that helped them reflect on their solution process, identify causes of errors, and generate actionable insights that can help them perform better over time. A pre-test/post-test and study and a survey indicate that Debriefly can improve students’ performance in the practiced subject matter as well as teach learners debriefing skills which learners perceive as useful and applicable to different learning contexts.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
